# Cursor AI Rules - React MUI Project
## 🤖 MANDATORY Rules for Cursor AI

> **CRITICAL**: This is a **STRICT RULEBOOK**. Any violation = code rejection.

## 📁 FOLDER STRUCTURE (MANDATORY)

```
src/
├── components/ui/[Name]/         # Reusable UI only
├── components/charts/[Name]/     # Charts only
├── features/[name]/              # Feature code (kebab-case)
│   ├── components/               # Feature components
│   ├── hooks/                    # Feature hooks
│   ├── store/                    # Feature state
│   └── services/                 # Feature APIs
├── shared/                       # Global shared
│   ├── store/                    # Global state
│   ├── hooks/                    # Global hooks
│   └── utils/                    # Utilities
├── theme/                        # MUI theme only
└── pages/                        # Page components
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: Wrong folder placement, nested folders >3 levels

## 🏷️ NAMING (MANDATORY)

| Type | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase | `LineChart.jsx` |
| Hooks | camelCase + "use" | `useChartData.js` |
| Stores | camelCase + "Store" | `chartStore.js` |
| Features | kebab-case | `user-management/` |
| Files | NO snake_case | ❌ `user_data.js` |
| JSX Files | .jsx extension | `Component.jsx` |

## ⚛️ COMPONENT RULES (MANDATORY)

```javascript
// REQUIRED: Every component must follow this pattern
// File name: Component.jsx (NOT .js)
import React from 'react'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const Component = React.memo(({ prop1, prop2 = 'default', ...props }) => {
  // 1. Hooks first
  const [state, setState] = useState()
  
  // 2. Memoized values
  const memoized = useMemo(() => calculation(prop1), [prop1])
  
  // 3. Callbacks
  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {}, [])
  
  // 4. Early returns
  if (!prop1) return null
  
  // 5. Render
  return <Box {...props}>Content</Box>
})

Component.propTypes = {
  prop1: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
  prop2: PropTypes.string,
}

export default Component
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: Class components, no React.memo, no PropTypes

## 🗄️ STATE MANAGEMENT (MANDATORY)

**Use Zustand Only** - Follow this pattern:

```javascript
import { create } from 'zustand'

export const useStore = create((set) => ({
  // State
  data: [],
  isLoading: false,
  error: null,
  
  // Actions
  setData: (data) => set({ data }),
  setLoading: (loading) => set({ isLoading: loading }),
  
  // Async
  fetchData: async () => {
    set({ isLoading: true, error: null })
    try {
      const data = await fetch('/api')
      set({ data, isLoading: false })
    } catch (error) {
      set({ error: error.message, isLoading: false })
    }
  }
}))
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: Redux, Context API for changing data, direct mutations

## 🎨 MUI USAGE (MANDATORY)

### Component Selection Rules:
```javascript
// Use Box for: Layout, spacing, flexbox
<Box sx={{ display: 'flex', gap: 2 }}>

// Use Paper for: Elevated surfaces  
<Paper elevation={1} sx={{ p: 2 }}>

// Use Card for: Content with actions
<Card>
  <CardContent>Content</CardContent>
  <CardActions><Button/></CardActions>
</Card>

// Use Grid for: Responsive layouts
<Grid container spacing={2}>
  <Grid item xs={12} md={6}>
```

### ❌ FORBIDDEN Nesting:
- Card inside Paper ❌
- Box inside Box without purpose ❌
- More than 3 levels deep ❌
- `style={}` prop ❌
- `className={}` prop ❌

### ✅ REQUIRED: Use sx prop only
```javascript
<Box sx={{ 
  p: 2,                                    // Use theme spacing
  backgroundColor: 'background.paper',      // Use theme colors
  [theme.breakpoints.down('md')]: { p: 1 } // Use theme breakpoints
}}>
```

## 📱 RESPONSIVE (MANDATORY)

```javascript
// REQUIRED: Mobile-first with theme breakpoints
<Box sx={{
  // Mobile default
  p: 1,
  fontSize: '0.875rem',
  
  // Tablet and up
  [theme.breakpoints.up('sm')]: {
    p: 2,
    fontSize: '1rem',
  },
  
  // Desktop and up
  [theme.breakpoints.up('md')]: {
    p: 3,
    fontSize: '1.125rem',
  },
}}>

// REQUIRED: Responsive Grid
<Grid container spacing={{ xs: 1, sm: 2, md: 3 }}>
  <Grid item xs={12} sm={6} md={4}>
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: Hardcoded breakpoints, px values without theme

## 📊 CHARTS (MANDATORY)

**Use MUI X Charts Only:**

```javascript
import { LineChart } from '@mui/x-charts/LineChart'

const Chart = React.memo(({ data, title, height = 400 }) => {
  const chartData = useMemo(() => ({
    series: data.series,
    xAxis: data.xAxis,
  }), [data])
  
  return (
    <Paper elevation={1} sx={{ p: 2, width: '100%' }}>
      <Typography variant="h6">{title}</Typography>
      <Box sx={{ height }}>
        <LineChart
          series={chartData.series}
          xAxis={chartData.xAxis}
          height={height}
        />
      </Box>
    </Paper>
  )
})
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: Other chart libraries, no memoization, hardcoded sizes

## 🚀 PERFORMANCE (MANDATORY)

```javascript
// REQUIRED: Always use these
const Component = React.memo(({ data, onClick }) => {
  // Memoize expensive calculations
  const processed = useMemo(() => data.map(transform), [data])
  
  // Memoize callbacks
  const handleClick = useCallback((id) => onClick(id), [onClick])
  
  // Memoize objects
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ option: 'value' }), [])
  
  return <Chart data={processed} onClick={handleClick} config={config} />
})
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: No React.memo, inline objects, no memoization

## 🔗 IMPORTS (MANDATORY)

```javascript
// REQUIRED: Follow this exact order
// 1. React
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react'

// 2. MUI
import { Box, Typography } from '@mui/material'
import { LineChart } from '@mui/x-charts/LineChart'

// 3. Internal (max 2 levels up)
import { useStore } from '../../store/chartStore'
import Button from '../ui/Button'

// 4. Types (if TypeScript)
import type { ChartData } from '../../types'
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: Wildcard imports, >2 levels up, wrong order

## 🧪 TESTING (MANDATORY)

```javascript
// REQUIRED: Every component needs tests
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import { ThemeProvider } from '@mui/material/styles'
import theme from '../../theme'

const renderWithTheme = (component) => 
  render(<ThemeProvider theme={theme}>{component}</ThemeProvider>)

describe('Component', () => {
  it('renders without crashing', () => {
    renderWithTheme(<Component />)
  })
  
  it('displays props correctly', () => {
    renderWithTheme(<Component title="Test" />)
    expect(screen.getByText('Test')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })
})
```

**❌ FORBIDDEN**: No tests, snapshot-only tests

## 🎯 THEME SETUP (MANDATORY)

```javascript
// src/theme/index.js - REQUIRED structure
import { createTheme } from '@mui/material/styles'

const theme = createTheme({
  spacing: 4,                    // Minimal spacing
  palette: {
    mode: 'light',
    primary: { main: '#1976d2' },
    background: {
      default: '#fafafa',
      paper: '#ffffff',
    },
  },
  components: {
    // Full-width containers
    MuiContainer: {
      styleOverrides: {
        root: {
          paddingLeft: 8,
          paddingRight: 8,
          maxWidth: '100% !important',
        },
      },
    },
  },
})

export default theme
```

